2.4-1 Circular - As a New Year gift to assessees, CBEC brought out this [Circular No. 967/1/2013-CX., dated 1-1-2013 seeking recovery of service tax pending stay applications filed by assessees. In view of the Circular, the recovery proceedings shall be initiated against a confirmed demand in terms of the following – 2.4-2 Circular read down - No recovery during pendency of stay application if delay in disposing of stay application not attributable to assessee - The said circular was challenged before various High Courts and read down as reported in -

Larsen and Tourbro Ltd. v. UOI [2013] 30 taxmann.com 363/38 STT 684 (Bom.) ;

PML Industries Ltd. (supra);

Gujarat State Fertilizer Co. Ltd. v. UOI 2013 (290) ELT 161 (Guj.) ;

Mangalam Cement Ltd. v. Superintendent, Central Excise [2013] 32 taxmann.com 52 (Raj.);

Metlife India Insurance Co. Ltd. v. UOI 2013 (290) ELT 362 (Kar.).

It has been held in aforesaid judgments that -

Sl. Nos. 3, 6, 9, 10 and 11 mandating initiation of recovery proceedings during pendency of stay application are invalid (though Sl. No. 11 was held valid in Gujarat State Fertilizer's case) ;

they cannot be applied to an assessee who has filed an application for stay, which has remained pending for reasons beyond his control. Assessee cannot be penalized without his fault or for circumstances outside his control ;

however, if application for stay had remained pending for more than a reasonable period, for reasons having a bearing on default/improper conduct of an assessee, recovery proceedings could very well be initiated.

